invariant: INV-14
file: cpu_cfg.h
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: cpu_cfg.h's x86-64 set loses CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA, so every init
  call of an x86-64 object refuses a caller that states AVX-512 IFMA, and
  a caller that copies its probe's answer into ch_cfg.cpu gets CH_EINVAL
  on such a CPU. On arm64 no test row moves, because that set is
  unchanged, so the catch is the script, which reads the header for both
  architectures and compares each set with the bits it writes out.

--- old
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA)
--- new
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256)
